WEBVTT

00:11.700 --> 00:13.050
Did you wait long?

00:16.200 --> 00:19.000
No, we only just arrived, too.

00:19.000 --> 00:20.670
Your Highness!

00:20.670 --> 00:22.290
Rimuru, what's this?

00:22.740 --> 00:26.300
I can't afford to have you pass out
thinking about how to make money,

00:26.300 --> 00:28.300
so I consulted King Gazel.

00:28.800 --> 00:33.300
I figured the king of the nation that
manufactures Dwarven gold coins could help.

00:33.700 --> 00:38.390
But I can only get you a little above
1,500 gold coins this sudden.

00:38.390 --> 00:39.940
That'd still be a great help.

00:40.400 --> 00:43.670
Will that be enough to pay
the merchants?

00:44.320 --> 00:46.280
Hmm...

00:46.280 --> 00:49.820
I only calculated it roughly in my head,
but I want a few hundred more.

00:50.200 --> 00:54.680
I'm shocked that you held a festival
this size with that level of accounting.

00:55.610 --> 00:57.520
We kinda make things up
along the way.

00:57.520 --> 01:00.490
We didn't have much time to set stuff up,
so what could I do?

01:00.490 --> 01:02.880
I don't even know
where to start to scold you about.

01:03.310 --> 01:06.880
I-I mean, everyone was
really into it and all.

01:07.260 --> 01:11.630
In that case, how about I make up
the difference for you?

01:14.770 --> 01:16.310
Ms. Elmesia?!

01:19.060 --> 01:19.810
Well, when I discussed it with Her Excellency,

01:19.810 --> 01:22.980
EPISODE 70: THE BATTLE WITH THE HERO
Well, when I discussed it with Her Excellency,

01:22.980 --> 01:23.860
EPISODE 70: THE BATTLE WITH THE HERO
she was delighted to offer help.

01:23.860 --> 01:25.770
she was delighted to offer help.

01:27.570 --> 01:29.780
It's fine, we'll be handling
this ourselves, so...

01:29.780 --> 01:31.530
Hm?

01:31.530 --> 01:35.030
I was only offering support
in light of the friendly relations

01:35.030 --> 01:37.290
our two countries will
share going forward.

01:37.760 --> 01:39.040
Uh, no, as I was saying...

01:39.480 --> 01:40.830
Give it up.

01:40.830 --> 01:44.210
Once that woman decides on something,
she'll not take no for an answer.

01:44.210 --> 01:47.210
You are better off accepting her offer.

01:47.670 --> 01:49.630
Oh my, Gazel boy.

01:49.630 --> 01:52.260
You're taking my side?

01:52.260 --> 01:53.800
That makes me so happy!

01:53.800 --> 01:56.510
Could you please stop calling me that?

01:56.510 --> 01:58.560
Gazel... boy...

01:58.560 --> 02:02.060
More importantly, what's your aim?

02:02.060 --> 02:04.560
You're always so stiff.

02:04.560 --> 02:08.229
Your grandfather
was much more freewheeling.

02:08.229 --> 02:11.690
Do you know how much hardship
my father went through because of that?

02:11.690 --> 02:14.990
Anyway, would you mind
getting down to business already?

02:15.450 --> 02:16.950
So hasty.

02:17.560 --> 02:20.330
Were you always
so impatient like that, hmm?

02:21.500 --> 02:23.290
Oh, may I have a drink as well?

02:23.290 --> 02:25.330
Yes, right away.

02:26.080 --> 02:28.540
Oh my, this is good.

02:28.540 --> 02:30.100
Thank you.

02:32.510 --> 02:37.970
Right, then. In exchange for providing
my support, I have one request.

02:39.890 --> 02:44.730
I cannot forgive you for planning
a festival this fun behind my back.

02:45.170 --> 02:47.400
If you promise to invite me
to future events,

02:47.400 --> 02:49.980
I would be happy to help
with this monetary exchange.

02:50.390 --> 02:52.240
I-I'd be glad to.

02:54.740 --> 02:57.370
Royalty aren't the slaves
of the people, you know.

02:57.790 --> 03:01.080
If they can live freely,
that makes their citizens happy as well...

03:01.080 --> 03:02.870
as it does me.

03:02.870 --> 03:05.290
I think it could help
bring joy to everyone.

03:07.420 --> 03:10.710
I agree. I believe so too.

03:10.710 --> 03:13.260
It's reassuring to have
people on my side,

03:13.260 --> 03:15.550
and I look forward
for it to stay that way.

03:19.890 --> 03:23.020
I only have my pocket money in here,

03:23.020 --> 03:25.770
so I only have around
a thousand gold coins.

03:26.690 --> 03:30.060
If you need more,
I could arrange for that, too.

03:30.060 --> 03:33.610
It's okay. That alone should
be enough for the meantime.

03:33.610 --> 03:37.070
Could we exchange
those for ten stellars, then?

03:37.070 --> 03:38.490
That's quite fine.

03:38.490 --> 03:40.870
Don't forget our promise, okay?

03:40.870 --> 03:42.330
Yes, of course.

03:42.330 --> 03:45.710
Now if we can get 1,500 gold coins
exchanged over at Dwargon,

03:45.710 --> 03:47.290
this problem will be behind us.

03:47.290 --> 03:49.670
How nice, Great Rimuru.

03:50.920 --> 03:56.010
This means the plan of whoever tries to make
a joke out of Great Rimuru has failed.

03:56.440 --> 03:59.680
But I think someone would
have offered their help

03:59.680 --> 04:02.510
even if you couldn't prepare
the gold coins in time.

04:02.510 --> 04:04.770
Hm? What do you mean?

04:05.310 --> 04:07.310
If you want someone
to do your bidding,

04:07.310 --> 04:10.900
rather than forcing your will
with fear or intimidation,

04:10.900 --> 04:14.280
it's far easier to have them
owe you a favor.

04:14.280 --> 04:15.900
I see.

04:15.900 --> 04:20.740
So someone uninvited might've swooped in
at the last minute to mediate for us, yes?

04:20.740 --> 04:22.029
Yes.

04:22.029 --> 04:23.910
That might be the case.

04:24.310 --> 04:29.670
But I believe even that someone will
likely be under another person's bidding.

04:31.500 --> 04:37.840
Causing the problem, then alleviating it
while creating an obligation for us.

04:37.840 --> 04:40.550
That does seem like a viable scheme.

04:40.550 --> 04:41.680
But...

04:42.160 --> 04:46.430
It would show the world leaders
that this nation cannot be trusted,

04:46.430 --> 04:49.190
and you would owe them a favor.

04:49.190 --> 04:54.110
How greedy.
Truly, a very human approach.

04:54.110 --> 04:55.690
I've learned a lot from this.

04:56.110 --> 04:59.740
Um, so, you're saying there could be
someone who caused this problem

04:59.740 --> 05:02.950
making us owe them
for helping us with it?

05:02.950 --> 05:05.240
I'm not too keen on these
kinds of matters,

05:05.240 --> 05:08.330
but is there someone you know
who'd do something like this?

05:08.330 --> 05:14.290
I wouldn't know.
Thalion isn't part of the Council, after all.

05:14.290 --> 05:15.340
But...

05:15.340 --> 05:18.840
maybe he would know something?

05:18.840 --> 05:21.090
Uh, me?!

05:22.220 --> 05:24.720
I have heard rumors.

05:24.720 --> 05:29.100
Rumors of a committee that controls
the Western Nations from the shadow.

05:29.480 --> 05:33.650
And they're likely the ringleader
behind this commotion?

05:35.440 --> 05:39.240
If someone suspicious shows up
and attempts to mediate with us...

05:39.240 --> 05:43.780
I will give them a thorough examination
and fully expose their backgrounds to you.

05:44.250 --> 05:47.990
What a shock.
I hardly detected his presence.

05:47.990 --> 05:50.290
This is why I told you,
Your Excellency.

05:50.670 --> 05:55.420
The denizens of this nation are abnormal,
so paying a visit in person is dangerous.

05:57.000 --> 06:00.170
But this is quite
an interesting experience.

06:00.600 --> 06:04.430
May I ask you a question, Sir Rimuru?

06:04.870 --> 06:06.680
Yes? What is it?

06:12.810 --> 06:16.860
I am considering enacting
a new pact with you.

06:17.350 --> 06:21.280
But before I do,
I want to hear your thoughts.

06:22.860 --> 06:24.530
Let's hear it.

06:24.530 --> 06:28.530
How do you plan to deal
with that demon over there?

06:29.160 --> 06:32.040
That incredibly dangerous primal one...

06:32.040 --> 06:33.790
Primal?

06:33.790 --> 06:35.540
Well, nothing, really.

06:35.540 --> 06:39.590
He is strong, but he's doing
a great deal of work for me,

06:39.590 --> 06:42.050
and I don't think he's all
that dangerous.

06:42.800 --> 06:44.930
Allow me to rephrase my question.

06:44.930 --> 06:49.850
How do you intend to take responsibility
would that demon run amok?

06:50.360 --> 06:51.470
Run amok?

06:51.470 --> 06:55.770
It's not unimaginable,
but it's a risk not limited to just Diablo.

06:55.770 --> 06:57.360
Like Shion, for example.

06:57.360 --> 07:00.480
I'll stop him before that happens,
of course.

07:00.480 --> 07:03.610
That's the only way
to prevent any fallout, isn't it?

07:05.110 --> 07:06.570
Why does he look so happy?

07:07.110 --> 07:10.120
Huh?! Um, what a minute.

07:10.120 --> 07:12.370
I couldn't even keep up the act.

07:12.370 --> 07:15.870
You would really stop that demon?
You're up for that responsibility?

07:15.870 --> 07:17.250
Yes.

07:17.250 --> 07:19.380
He did go a bit too far
here and there,

07:19.380 --> 07:22.710
but he's started listening
to me more lately.

07:22.710 --> 07:25.760
I think he's much calmer than before.

07:25.760 --> 07:28.720
Oh my. Did you hear that, Erald?

07:28.720 --> 07:32.520
This Demon Lord's an even bigger
piece of work than how you described him!

07:32.520 --> 07:34.020
Y-Yes...

07:34.020 --> 07:36.980
That should be enough, Lady Elmesia.

07:36.980 --> 07:40.480
If that's what he said,
then I'll support him.

07:40.480 --> 07:42.530
Should things get dire...

07:43.070 --> 07:47.530
I promise you that I, Gazel Dwargon,
will come to Rimuru's aid.

07:49.440 --> 07:52.240
I understand your thoughts now.

07:52.240 --> 07:55.000
If you should ever become
an enemy to mankind,

07:55.000 --> 07:58.790
I will exercise all my force to stop you.

07:58.790 --> 08:01.590
Let us continue to maintain
our current friendly relations

08:01.590 --> 08:04.550
and deepen the bonds of our nations.

08:04.550 --> 08:06.380
- Erlad.
- Yes, Your Excellency.

08:06.380 --> 08:10.890
I hereby officially acknowledge
the friendship relation between

08:10.890 --> 08:14.180
Sorcerous Dynasty of Thalion
and Jura-Tempest Federation.

08:14.630 --> 08:17.020
Please handle the paperwork for me.

08:17.020 --> 08:17.940
Yes, Your Excellency.

08:17.940 --> 08:22.520
Well, should anything come up,
feel free to confer with me or lil' Gazel.

08:22.520 --> 08:24.440
Don't let yourself go
out of control, okay?

08:24.870 --> 08:29.410
Hey, I'm a pretty prudent person,
you know?

08:29.820 --> 08:35.409
Rimuru, could you remind me who decided to
hold this Founder's Festival out of whim?

08:35.409 --> 08:37.409
It was you, right, Mjöllmile?

08:37.409 --> 08:39.789
No, it wasn't me, Great Rimuru.

08:39.789 --> 08:42.169
Okay, I know. I get it.

08:42.169 --> 08:45.300
I'll consult about it first
from here on out.

08:45.300 --> 08:49.720
Normally it's not right to say this
to the king of another nation,

08:49.720 --> 08:51.680
but you're a special case.

08:51.680 --> 08:54.680
That's right.
I hope you will.

08:54.680 --> 08:58.560
Oh, speaking of that, I have another
important thing to discuss with you.

08:58.560 --> 09:01.190
Um, are there other problems?

09:01.190 --> 09:04.520
No, it's not exactly a problem.

09:04.520 --> 09:07.490
This is just a personal wish,

09:07.490 --> 09:09.780
but I hope you can introduce me
to Mr. Yoshida.

09:09.780 --> 09:14.450
Your Excellency! How could you sneak
that topic into a serious talk like this?

09:14.450 --> 09:17.240
That'd be no problem.

09:17.240 --> 09:20.750
Just promise me you won't
force Mr. Yoshida anything, okay?

09:20.750 --> 09:23.000
Of course!

09:24.250 --> 09:25.210
And so,

09:25.210 --> 09:31.800
the midnight three-way summit between
three large nations came to a close.

09:34.550 --> 09:38.140
Now's finally the time
for the final match!

09:38.140 --> 09:41.810
Which of these two will seize
the glory of victory?!

09:41.810 --> 09:44.480
Will it be the Lightspeed Masayuki,
or perhaps...

09:44.480 --> 09:49.030
Gobta, the small warrior
who rose up as a Big Four candidate?

09:49.030 --> 09:52.320
D-Doesn't seem like
I can run away from this.

09:52.320 --> 09:56.160
In that case, I'll try to win this
and get that latest fishing rod!

09:59.370 --> 10:02.540
What do I do? What can I do
to survive this? Like hell I can win!

10:02.540 --> 10:05.000
If I had fought that
monster Bovix yesterday,

10:05.000 --> 10:06.710
I bet he would've
killed me like a fly!

10:06.710 --> 10:07.800
No, wait...

10:07.800 --> 10:09.430
Well then...

10:09.430 --> 10:11.050
Let's begin!

10:11.050 --> 10:12.130
That's right!

10:12.130 --> 10:16.470
My power that makes other people convinced
on their own worked just fine yesterday.

10:16.900 --> 10:18.850
I'm sure things will work out today, too.

10:18.850 --> 10:19.470
Fight!

10:21.740 --> 10:23.600
Here I go!

10:28.770 --> 10:32.900
Whoaa! Is handsomeness
the proof of strength, after all?

10:33.290 --> 10:36.160
Paying no heed
to Gobta's tricky maneuvers,

10:36.160 --> 10:39.200
Masayuki appears to be completely unfazed!

10:40.950 --> 10:44.290
H-Heh, this much is expected.

10:46.000 --> 10:50.050
You're acting like nothing
I can do will hit you, huh?

10:50.630 --> 10:55.050
I wanted to see just how far I could
go with my own strength today...

10:55.050 --> 10:57.550
But I'll be using it today!

10:57.550 --> 11:00.390
My new, ultimate power!

11:00.390 --> 11:04.390
Come to think of it, Raphael was
trying to say something yesterday.

11:05.060 --> 11:05.850
Report.

11:05.850 --> 11:11.440
Last night, the subject Gobta obtained
the Unique skill Summon Demon Wolf.

11:11.440 --> 11:15.780
Subject Ranga forcing himself into
yesterday's summoning is likely the cause,

11:15.780 --> 11:19.410
but he can now unite with
the summoned Ranga.

11:19.410 --> 11:21.700
Unite with Ranga?

11:21.700 --> 11:24.410
Can he really use it properly
without any practice?

11:25.500 --> 11:27.040
Look and behold!

11:27.670 --> 11:28.960
Transform!

11:46.730 --> 11:51.020
Hold on, what on earth is that?!
Nobody told me about this!

11:51.690 --> 11:54.230
If he were to gouge me
with those large claws,

11:54.230 --> 11:57.320
he'd scrap my whole body along
with this cheap armor like paper!

11:57.320 --> 12:03.450
W-Wow! So cool! What's that?!
It's so cool!

12:04.580 --> 12:06.500
L-Look at that!

12:06.500 --> 12:10.250
Gobta has transformed into
something far from himself!

12:10.250 --> 12:12.870
It is a very rare skill
that lets you infuse your own body

12:12.870 --> 12:14.590
with the power of a summoned creature.

12:14.590 --> 12:19.720
That means Gobta is wielding
Ranga's power as his own right now!

12:19.720 --> 12:23.510
Amazing! We're witnessing
something amazing here, folks!

12:23.510 --> 12:25.520
Exciting! So exciting!

12:26.600 --> 12:29.810
So that means he can freely
use Ranga's power?

12:30.440 --> 12:33.440
Ranga seems to be
giving himself up to Gobta,

12:33.440 --> 12:36.320
but this combo might work
a lot better than expected.

12:36.320 --> 12:38.530
But it's Gobta we're talking about.

12:39.540 --> 12:41.570
In spite of it all,
he's still my apprentice.

12:41.570 --> 12:44.510
He may be lacking in physical strength,
but has more than enough

12:44.510 --> 12:47.450
experience fighting majins stronger
than himself to make up for it.

12:47.450 --> 12:53.960
If he could wield Ranga's power well,
he might show an unexpected growth.

12:55.210 --> 12:58.260
Heh-heh! Now it's my turn!

12:58.260 --> 13:01.990
It's been your turn since the start.
Masayuki-kun hasn't done anything yet.

13:05.560 --> 13:06.720
Hold on! I surre...

13:14.820 --> 13:18.780
Whoa! Is Gobta and Ranga okay?

13:18.780 --> 13:21.610
What just happened?

13:22.490 --> 13:24.410
That idiot.

13:24.410 --> 13:27.580
Looks like he couldn't wield
Ranga's power well enough.

13:28.870 --> 13:34.460
That guy! After looking all cool
like that... What was that mess?

13:34.460 --> 13:39.170
There, there. Gobta was doing
his best in his own ways, okay?

13:39.170 --> 13:44.090
Rimuru, you're not doing anything
good for him if you keep spoiling him.

13:44.090 --> 13:46.180
That's right, Great Rimuru.

13:46.180 --> 13:49.850
It appeared I might have spoiled Gobta
a little too much for his own good.

13:49.850 --> 13:51.440
You count THAT as spoiling him?!

13:51.830 --> 13:54.440
All right! I'll train him well!

13:54.440 --> 13:57.360
Rimuru, let me take care of Gobta
for a while.

13:57.770 --> 14:01.150
I'll sure raise him
into a fine warrior!

14:01.150 --> 14:03.360
My condolences, Gobta.

14:11.120 --> 14:15.380
That must have been
Sir Masayuki's air throw.

14:15.380 --> 14:17.750
Y-Yeah, that has to be.

14:17.750 --> 14:20.340
Whoa! Amazing! That was amazing!

14:20.340 --> 14:21.760
I didn't see it at all!

14:23.510 --> 14:26.720
Of course you didn't see it.
I didn't do a thing!

14:26.720 --> 14:28.890
There was no dodging that one.

14:28.890 --> 14:30.520
If he actually hit me with that...

14:30.520 --> 14:32.730
The judgment is in!

14:32.730 --> 14:35.980
And while I'm concerned for
the still-unconscious Gobta...

14:35.980 --> 14:38.490
This is bad! They'll declare me
the winner at this rate!

14:38.490 --> 14:41.180
The right to challenge a Demon Lord?
You got to be kidding me!

14:41.180 --> 14:42.690
That's nothing but suicide!

14:42.690 --> 14:44.110
The winner is...

14:44.110 --> 14:44.980
Wait.

14:46.450 --> 14:48.530
Huh? U-Um...

14:49.490 --> 14:53.500
I lost this match, I suppose.

14:55.250 --> 14:58.460
Um, excuse me, Sir Masayuki.

14:58.460 --> 15:02.130
Gobta very clearly took
himself out of the match...

15:02.630 --> 15:04.260
That might be true.

15:04.260 --> 15:08.300
But I wasn't able to keep up
with his attack.

15:08.300 --> 15:12.890
My inability to do so shows that it's still
too early for me to challenge a Demon Lord.

15:17.400 --> 15:20.270
My power should still be in effect.

15:20.270 --> 15:23.280
If I just shut my mouth,
the audience will imagine stuff

15:23.280 --> 15:25.110
and get convinced on their own.

15:25.650 --> 15:28.950
More importantly, I must get out
of this place as soon as possible.

15:29.380 --> 15:31.700
What is he thinking?

15:33.080 --> 15:34.330
I don't know.

15:34.330 --> 15:37.460
It wasn't like he got
scared of Gobta or anything.

15:37.460 --> 15:38.960
Just what is he after?

15:39.480 --> 15:42.200
Is it because he can't go full strength
against the Demon Lord?

15:42.200 --> 15:45.590
Nah, he was just being humble when he said
he couldn't keep up with his attack.

15:45.590 --> 15:47.130
I see! I get it now!

15:47.720 --> 15:50.800
Maybe Sir Masayuki just gave
the Demon Lord a reprieve?

15:50.800 --> 15:52.430
What do you mean?

15:52.430 --> 15:55.350
He's giving the Demon Lord's
underlings the spotlights

15:55.350 --> 15:58.980
to send a message that "I could win
the tournament whenever I like.

15:58.980 --> 16:02.230
If you dare to do anything bad,
I won't stay put."

16:02.230 --> 16:05.610
I see. Now that you say it,
it does make sense.

16:05.610 --> 16:08.950
Sir Masayuki didn't unsheathe
his sword this time, either, did he?

16:08.950 --> 16:11.780
Well spotted. You're right.

16:11.780 --> 16:14.620
What a wonderful young man!

16:14.620 --> 16:16.160
That's the Sir Masayuki I know!

16:16.910 --> 16:19.670
He is so cool!

16:19.670 --> 16:30.220
Masayuki! Masayuki! Masayuki!

16:30.640 --> 16:31.970
What the heck is this?

16:31.970 --> 16:33.970
Why is the audience
cheering on him so much?

16:33.970 --> 16:35.060
Answer.

16:35.060 --> 16:37.860
It is predicted to be the effect of
the Unique skill

16:37.860 --> 16:39.690
possessed by the subject Masayuki Honjo.

16:39.690 --> 16:42.190
It appears to be affecting
the emotions of those around

16:42.190 --> 16:45.230
and manipulating them
akin to mind control.

16:45.230 --> 16:47.820
Its effect is tremendous.

16:47.820 --> 16:53.240
That means he's the type you don't want to
mess with, or rather, better befriend with.

16:53.240 --> 16:54.620
Soei.

16:54.620 --> 16:55.080
Yes, sir.

16:55.480 --> 16:59.830
Tell Masayuki that I'd like to
invite him for lunch after this.

16:59.830 --> 17:01.210
Keep it courteous, okay?

17:01.210 --> 17:02.580
Understood, sir.

17:03.250 --> 17:05.839
Today's been a series
of unexpected events,

17:05.839 --> 17:10.339
but with Masayuki's withdrawal,
Gobta is our champion!

17:11.339 --> 17:14.430
Now, Gobta.
How are you feeling right now?

17:14.430 --> 17:16.099
Huh? What?

17:16.099 --> 17:17.810
For real?

17:19.310 --> 17:21.099
I won?!

17:21.560 --> 17:22.770
That's right!

17:22.770 --> 17:26.359
You put in an excellent
performance today!

17:27.109 --> 17:29.360
We will now move on
to the award ceremony!

17:32.020 --> 17:34.450
To our second place, Hero Masayuki!

17:34.450 --> 17:36.410
I hereby praise your accomplishment today!

17:38.620 --> 17:41.000
Th-Thank you very much.

17:41.000 --> 17:43.380
Also, I'll oblige to your invitation.

17:43.380 --> 17:46.420
He looked resolute
for whatever reason.

17:46.420 --> 17:49.130
He didn't get any wrong idea, did he?

17:50.260 --> 17:51.930
You did great, Gobta.

17:51.930 --> 17:56.430
With this, I hereby officially declare you
a member of the Big Four.

17:56.430 --> 17:58.430
Thank you!

17:58.430 --> 18:00.430
I'll do my best from here on out!

18:00.430 --> 18:04.940
Uh, yeah, I think you'll need to
start doing that right after this.

18:04.940 --> 18:05.940
What?

18:05.940 --> 18:07.070
Can I take him now?

18:08.070 --> 18:11.530
Well then, I'll start training him now.

18:11.960 --> 18:13.280
Don't overdo it, okay?

18:13.280 --> 18:15.280
Just relax.

18:15.280 --> 18:19.040
I'll train him inside the labyrinth,
so even if he dies, he'll be right back up.

18:19.040 --> 18:20.120
Train?

18:20.120 --> 18:23.790
Wait, Lady Milim!
I didn't ask for that at all!

18:23.790 --> 18:26.250
Gobta, this is a good opportunity,

18:26.250 --> 18:30.300
so give it your best training
under Lady Milim's tutelage.

18:30.300 --> 18:33.800
M-Master! Did you sell me off?!

18:33.800 --> 18:34.970
Oh, shut up.

18:34.970 --> 18:36.510
My Master!

18:36.510 --> 18:39.850
My teamwork with Sir Gobta
brought us the championship!

18:40.250 --> 18:41.850
He abandoned Gobta so casually.

18:41.850 --> 18:42.680
Hold it.

18:43.520 --> 18:47.150
Gobta's training won't
be complete without you.

18:47.150 --> 18:52.150
Wahahaha! I'll treat you both well,
so rest assured!

18:52.150 --> 18:54.150
C'mon, let's go!

18:54.530 --> 18:57.950
Goodbye, Gobta.
Goodbye, Ranga.

18:57.950 --> 19:00.160
I'll forever remember your bravery.

19:03.910 --> 19:07.380
G-Good to make your
acquaintance, I guess?

19:07.380 --> 19:11.420
People call me "Lightspeed" and "Hero"
and stuff. My name's Honjo Masayuki.

19:11.420 --> 19:15.510
Well, this is not the first time we've met,
but nice to meet you.

19:15.510 --> 19:18.800
I'm Demon Lord Rimuru.
My real name is Satoru Mikami.

19:18.800 --> 19:20.930
I'm a former office worker.

19:20.930 --> 19:24.060
A-Are you a Japanese?

19:24.060 --> 19:27.060
Well, yeah.
Let's talk about that while we eat.

19:27.690 --> 19:30.070
I-Is it really okay for me to eat this?

19:30.070 --> 19:31.650
Of course!

19:31.650 --> 19:34.820
I had them whip up
Japanese food for you.

19:35.240 --> 19:36.990
For my last meal?

19:36.990 --> 19:38.570
No, it isn't.

19:38.570 --> 19:42.990
I just want to get along with you,
coming from the same place and all.

19:44.580 --> 19:47.330
Then... Don't mind if I do.

19:47.330 --> 19:49.000
Okay, let's eat.

19:58.510 --> 20:01.180
I'm glad he liked it.

20:01.180 --> 20:05.020
It'd be bad to bug him now.
I'll save the talk until he's done.

20:07.770 --> 20:09.020
I understand.

20:09.020 --> 20:12.770
Mikami, I mean, Mr. Rimuru.
I'll be happy to be your servant.

20:12.770 --> 20:14.780
Servant? Uh...

20:14.780 --> 20:16.820
No, it's fine.

20:16.820 --> 20:19.740
I don't care much about
my status as a Hero.

20:19.740 --> 20:23.790
To be frank, it's a little embarrassing
to have people cheer my name so often.

20:24.410 --> 20:25.290
Please.

20:26.540 --> 20:30.960
I've been constantly trying to figure out
how to get myself out of the situation.

20:30.960 --> 20:33.960
He sure doesn't hide
anything from me, huh.

20:33.960 --> 20:38.970
My Unique skill's called
"Chosen One," you know?

20:38.970 --> 20:41.140
Can you believe that?

20:41.140 --> 20:44.970
Like I want to be a hero just because
I like reading manga and light novels.

20:45.460 --> 20:47.100
So even though you don't want it,

20:47.100 --> 20:50.480
other people and your surroundings
keep making you the hero, huh?

20:50.920 --> 20:53.020
But still, what a skill.

20:53.020 --> 20:56.190
If you hadn't resigned back then,
you would've won.

20:56.190 --> 21:00.740
Even that Gobta guy turned
into such a fearsome form.

21:00.740 --> 21:04.240
Any normal person could tell
there's no winning against him.

21:04.240 --> 21:09.000
But you promised a rematch
with Bovix, right? What'll you do?

21:09.000 --> 21:10.750
Are you going to tackle the dungeon?

21:12.000 --> 21:14.210
Wh-What should I do?

21:14.210 --> 21:19.300
Don't worry.
Bovix only guards the 50th floor.

21:19.300 --> 21:23.680
The dungeon's super large, so it's gonna
take several days just to make it that far.

21:23.680 --> 21:28.980
S-So if I pretend to tackle it,
I'll at least make it through today?

21:28.980 --> 21:30.660
That's right.

21:31.310 --> 21:33.230
That's also where I want your help.

21:33.230 --> 21:36.650
I'd like you to help advertise
the merit of conquering the dungeon.

21:36.650 --> 21:39.740
I'll guarantee your
and your friends' safety, of course.

21:39.740 --> 21:41.860
That's perfect.

21:41.860 --> 21:46.120
If there's no risk of dying,
I can tackle it worry-free.

21:46.120 --> 21:49.500
Just use the hints I give you
to tackle the dungeon.

21:49.500 --> 21:52.080
Also, if you see anything
you think we could improve,

21:52.080 --> 21:53.790
don't be shy about telling me.

21:53.790 --> 21:55.500
Understood.

21:55.500 --> 21:58.800
It sounds like doing
a test play for a game.

21:59.270 --> 22:02.760
Yeah, it is kinda like that
now that you mentioned it.

22:02.760 --> 22:07.310
Well, no need to knock yourself out today.
Just try to reach Floor 5 or something.

22:07.310 --> 22:08.720
All right.

22:08.720 --> 22:11.020
I'm glad we got to talk today.

22:11.020 --> 22:12.810
It really put my mind at ease,

22:12.810 --> 22:15.810
and I'm starting to think this
world isn't so bad after all.

22:15.810 --> 22:19.820
Like I said before, you're free to stay
in this town for as long as you want,

22:19.820 --> 22:21.570
so let's keep in touch, okay?

22:21.570 --> 22:23.530
I can?!

22:23.530 --> 22:26.160
There are toilets and baths,
so it's really nice in here!

22:26.530 --> 22:29.410
We have an orchestra,
and we're teaching people how to paint.

22:29.410 --> 22:32.160
I plan to get some theater
productions going eventually, too.

22:32.580 --> 22:37.130
I want to have fun here, and I'm not
gonna skimp on investing in that stuff.

22:37.130 --> 22:39.670
I really respect you, Mr. Rimuru!

22:39.670 --> 22:42.170
Ah, what about manga?

22:43.380 --> 22:45.260
Of course that, too,
my friend Masayuki.

22:45.260 --> 22:47.470
It's a long road ahead,

22:47.470 --> 22:49.680
but who else gonna do it?

22:51.100 --> 22:53.980
I'll follow you wherever you go,
Mr. Rimuru!

22:54.690 --> 22:58.110
And like that, I got myself a new friend.

22:58.690 --> 23:01.820
I'm also interested in the manga
he has stored in his brain,

23:01.820 --> 23:05.070
so I'd like to get along
with him from now on.

24:35.950 --> 24:39.170
Next time,
"The Labyrinth's Grand Opening."
